      "rows": [
        {
          "dimension": "Centralization",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "The Foundation's Delegation Program controls meaningful validator economics; its active rotation and expulsion powers demonstrate concentrated influence over network topology even as it claims to be reducing it.",
          "source": "https://solana.com/news/solana-foundation-delegation-program-case-study"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Smart-contract / Protocol Security",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "The launch of STRIDE (24/7 monitoring above $10M TVL) and SIRN (formal verification above $100M TVL) was a direct response to high-profile exploits like the $270M Drift incident, indicating the ecosystem's security baseline required Foundation-level intervention to shore up.",
          "source": "https://whale-alert.io/stories/91a2019022e8d8/Solana-Foundation-launches-STRIDE-and-SIRN-days-after-270M-Drift-exploit"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Regulatory",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "The VARA cooperation deal in Dubai and x402 Foundation membership signal proactive regulatory positioning, but the Foundation's active endorsement of a public-company treasury takeover introduces regulatory surface area around securities treatment of SOL.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Liquidity",
          "level": "Low",
          "note": "The Foundation's direct USDT loan to Aave to ease a liquidity crunch at launch reflects both capability and a willingness to act as a backstop, reducing acute DeFi liquidity risk on-chain while creating a mild moral-hazard precedent.",
          "source": "https://solanafloor.com/news/solana-foundation-joins-fight-to-save-defi-lends-usdt-on-aave"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Slashing / Validator Penalties",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Removal of operators from the Delegation Program for sandwich attacks establishes a de-facto penalty regime not encoded in the base protocol, creating ambiguity about due process and appeal paths for validators.",
          "source": "https://solana.com/news/solana-foundation-delegation-program-case-study"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Market / Competitive",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Senior talent departures to rival L1 ecosystems (ZKsync) and the Foundation's own president declaring crypto gaming dead suggest honest acknowledgment of failed verticals but also competitive erosion at the leadership layer.",
          "source": ""
        }
